{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Swami","externalID":"Swami","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state graph rather than imperative functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"native SwiftUI construct maps cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"helper, Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Corpus (in progress — 2 of 69)","anchor":"Corpus-in-progress-2-of-69"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The translated corpus is the gallery and the training set. Each entry is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verified SwiftUI translation of an Origami pattern."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Interaction","anchor":"Interaction"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:Interaction_Touch"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_Drag","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text",